{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1Ju55ZThNLfy6tFPAsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm recommending **GO** for payload 13/32. It adds two new files, `_lib/agent_spawn/prompt_rules.py` and `skill_reference.py`, and both are verbatim moves out of `check_agent_spawn.py` that behave the same at runtime. No declared condition is false against them, and there is no P0 and no new P1. I found four P2 follow-ups, all low-impact.\n\nWhat I checked:\n- **Same text as before the split.** I compared both files against the older copy at `.claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1/tree/.claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py` and they match line for line. That copy is a staged plan snapshot, not the `v1.4.3-rc.1` tag itself, so the match is to that snapshot.\n- **Every name they rely on exists at runtime.** Neither file imports what it uses. The hook loads both into its own namespace (`install()` for `prompt_rules`, `bind()` for `skill_reference`), and every outside name they need is defined there. All names listed in each file's `__all__` exist, and none clash with the other parts.\n- **No new import failure.** Both files load cleanly on their own under Python 3.9, using only the standard library (`re`).\n- **Failure still allows the session.** If a component is missing, the hook prints `{}` and exits 0, or `main()` allows the spawn. That is the correct direction for an infrastructure fault. The checks that block on bad input (prompt defense, file assignment, skill reference) are unchanged, and tests exercise their block paths.\n- **Adopters get the files and they are protected.** `install.sh` and `upgrade.sh` ship `_lib/agent_spawn/`, and `check_arbitration_kernel.py:310` lists it as a kernel path. Neither file writes anything except audit events.\n\nP2 follow-ups (all carried over unchanged from before the split):\n1. **Comments promise behavior the code lacks.** `prompt_rules.py:168-170` and `:213-214` say `CEO_SPAWN_SECRET_SCAN=0` is a logged kill-switch and that \"any non-0 value enforces\". The code is off by default, scans only when the value is exactly `\"1\"` (line 221), and the `spawn_secret_scan_bypassed` event exists nowhere. Fix: rewrite the comment and docstring.\n2. **Two checks ignore the environment passed to `decide()`.** `prompt_rules.py:221` and `skill_reference.py:282-284` read `os.environ` directly. So the MCP handler or a test that supplies its own environment or project directory doesn't affect these checks. Fix: pass `src_env` and `repo_root` through.\n3. **A future rename could silently disable two blocking checks.** `_enforce_prompt_defense` and `_enforce_spawn_rails` catch every exception and allow. If a shared name were renamed, the error would be swallowed and the check would quietly turn into an allow. Fix: add a test that every global each part uses resolves in the hook.\n4. **Stale comments.**\n   - `prompt_rules.py:364` says \"below\", but the value comes from another file.\n   - `prompt_rules.py:397-404` describes a constant that is actually inline at `file_assignment.py:496`.\n   - In another payload, `check_agent_spawn.py:601-602` still points to \"check_agent_spawn.py:188\" for the `REASON_REFERENCE_*` constants, which now live at `prompt_rules.py:93-105`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":125009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1099},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59b5611e-09e0-46d4-995f-7512413afb4d","uuid":"81fe74ff-03d4-4b2e-8555-a5f288f31021","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:19:32.461Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1Ju4suMn7R4T3peJi5k"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1Ju55ZThNLfy6tFPAsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011nJAa4sTi4PW1SphtMrQKV","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 13/32 - SCOPE: two new files, .claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/prompt_rules.py (559 lines) and .claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/skill_reference.py (319 lines), part of the PLAN-197 split of check_agent_spawn.py (conditions 5 and 7).\n\nWHAT WAS VERIFIED (against the candidate tree)\n1. Same text as before the split. Every function and constant in both files is textually identical to the copy before the split at .claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1/tree/.claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py (lines 969-1489, 1508-1792, 2208-2360). That includes the secret-pattern catalog, the PEM regex, the 12 reason codes, _FA_FENCE_RE, the prompt-defense hint set and the kill-switch semantics. Limit: that file is a staged plan snapshot, not the v1.4.3-rc.1 tag itself; the identity is to that snapshot.\n2. Every free name resolves. Neither file imports what it uses (skill_reference imports nothing; prompt_rules imports only re). check_agent_spawn.py:137-139 loads model_routing, advisories and prompt_rules through _lib._audit_emit_parts.install, which rebinds each function onto the hook's globals and deep-copies the non-function values. check_agent_spawn.py:641-647 binds skill_reference and file_assignment through _lib/agent_spawn/__init__.py:bind. Every free name these files use exists in the hook namespace at call time:\n   - _HTML_COMMENT_RE, _CODE_FENCE_RE, _NEXT_H2_RE, _SKILL_CONTENT_MARKER_RE and _SKILL_CONTENT_MIN_BYTES come from advisories.__all__ (advisories.py:5);\n   - os, re, hashlib, unicodedata, Path, _redact, _audit_emit and _AUDIT_EMIT_AVAILABLE come from the hook (check_agent_spawn.py:39-79);\n   - the REASON_* constants and the _SKILL_REFERENCE_* regexes come from prompt_rules.\n   All 63 names in prompt_rules.__all__ and all 10 in skill_reference.__all__ are defined. No name appears in two parts' __all__, and none collides with a definition in the hook itself.\n3. Import safety. Both files import cleanly on their own. The module-level annotations (List[...], re.Pattern[str]) stay as strings under `from __future__ import annotations`. Regex patterns deep-copy as themselves on 3.7+. Standard library only; compatible with Python 3.9.\n4. Fail direction. A component that fails to import gives `{}` and exit 0 under __main__ (check_agent_spawn.py:126-135), or main() allows when _SPAWN_COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR is set (entrypoint.py:12-16). Both fail OPEN on an infrastructure fault. The input-side blocks are unchanged: matched hint plus missing PROMPT DEFENSE block blocks, and the SKILL REFERENCE sub-checks fail CLOSED. Their block paths are exercised by test_prompt_defense_baseline.py and test_check_agent_spawn_file_assignment.py.\n5. Adopter blast radius. install.sh walks _lib/* and upgrade.sh uses the exclusion-based _framework_path_excluded, so _lib/agent_spawn/ ships. check_arbitration_kernel.py:310 lists \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\", which is consistent with condition 5. Neither file writes anything except audit emits. No model, effort or default changes.\n\nP0: none.\nP1: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (all carried verbatim from before the split; none introduced by this delta)\n- P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/prompt_rules.py:168-170 and :213-214 - honesty drift. The comment promises a CEO_SPAWN_SECRET_SCAN=0 kill-switch \"logged via veto_triggered(reason_code=spawn_secret_scan_bypassed)\", and the docstring says \"any non-0 value enforces\". The code (line 221) is default-OFF, enforces only on the exact value \"1\", and spawn_secret_scan_bypassed exists nowhere. Failure scenario: an operator who sets CEO_SPAWN_SECRET_SCAN=true believes the scan is armed; it is not. Minimal fix: rewrite the comment and docstring to \"opt-in, exact value 1; no bypass event\".\n- P2 prompt_rules.py:221 and skill_reference.py:282-284 - both read os.environ instead of the env dict passed to decide(). Callers such as the MCP handler or tests that supply an env or project_dir do not affect the secret-scan opt-in or the SKILL REFERENCE repo_root. Minimal fix: pass src_env (and a repo_root derived from it) from decide().\n- P2 fragile coupling. _enforce_prompt_defense (prompt_rules.py:527-559) and _enforce_spawn_rails (file_assignment.py:383-504) wrap their bodies in `except Exception: return None`. Their correctness now depends on implicit globals supplied by other parts. A future rename that drops one of those names would turn an input-side fail-CLOSED gate into a silent allow: the NameError would be swallowed as an \"infra fault\". Minimal fix: add a static test that walks co_names for every function bound from _lib/agent_spawn/* and asserts that each global resolves in the check_agent_spawn namespace.\n- P2 stale comments:\n  - prompt_rules.py:364 says _OVERLAP_LOOKBACK_S is re-exported \"below\"; it is bound later from file_assignment.py:7.\n  - prompt_rules.py:397-404 is an orphan comment for a read-only marker constant that lives inline at file_assignment.py:496.\n  - (other payload) check_agent_spawn.py:601-602 still points at \"check_agent_spawn.py:188 REASON_REFERENCE_*\"; those constants are now at prompt_rules.py:93-105.\n  Minimal fix: update the pointers.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Both new files are verbatim moves out of check_agent_spawn.py; every name they rely on resolves in the hook, failure still allows the session, the package is a kernel path that ships to adopters, and the only findings are carried-over P2 comment and coupling notes, so no declared condition is false and there is no P0."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":125009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp